  "question": {
    "text": "There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> players in a cricket team, out of which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> are bowlers, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> are batsmen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> are wicketkeepers. The number of ways, a team of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>&nbsp;players be selected from them so as to include at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> bowlers, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> batsmen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> wicketkeeper, is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "777",
